---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="The story behind Lost Hiker Coffee Roasters — Jordan and Leah, roasting in Sayward, BC.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">Our Story</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Where the trail led us.</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">We're Jordan and Leah, the owners, founders, roasters, packers, salespeople, taste testers, and just about everything else behind Lost Hiker Coffee Roasters in Sayward, BC.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div class="story-image sticky-image">
        <img src="/images/leahjordan.jpg" alt="Leah and Jordan, co-founders of Lost Hiker Coffee Roasters" />
      </div>
      <div class="story-text">

        <h2>How it started</h2>
        <p>Our story started long before Lost Hiker had a name.</p>
        <p>Years ago, Jordan was invited into the home of an Eritrean family and watched them roast coffee the traditional way, right in a pan in their kitchen. The experience stayed with him, and so did the idea of roasting coffee ourselves.</p>
        <p>At the same time, we had always been drawn to quieter places. Some of our favourite time together has been spent camping, exploring logging roads, and finding beautiful spots off the beaten path.</p>
        <p>Eventually, that pull toward a simpler, more remote life brought us to Sayward. Once we were here, the idea of roasting coffee finally felt like it had found the right home.</p>

        <h2>From a Whirley Pop to Lost Hiker</h2>
        <p>Life in Sayward has a different rhythm. We grow some of our own food, forage, make things ourselves, and spend a lot of time surrounded by the wild beauty of northern Vancouver Island. Roasting our own coffee felt like a natural extension of that way of life, especially in a place where freshly roasted coffee isn't something you can simply pick up around the corner.</p>
        <p>So we started with a Whirley Pop and a lot of experimenting.</p>
        <p>Friends and family became our first taste testers, bringing encouragement, honest opinions, and very different ideas about what a great cup of coffee should taste like. Eventually, that same community came together to help us purchase a real coffee roaster and turn a long-held interest into Lost Hiker Coffee Roasters.</p>
        <p>Today, every batch is roasted in our roasting studio here on our property in Sayward. That spirit of experimentation still shapes what we roast, with our coffees growing through tasting, feedback, tinkering, and the simple pleasure of sharing a good cup with the people around us.</p>

        <h2>Why Lost Hiker?</h2>
        <p>Our roasting studio sits on our property near the end of the Kusam Climb. Every year, hikers make their way past us after coming down from Mount Kusam, the same mountain you'll find in the Lost Hiker logo.</p>
        <p>The name felt right for more than that reason.</p>
        <p>We've always loved wandering, exploring, taking the long way, and finding beautiful things where you weren't necessarily looking for them. To us, getting a little lost isn't always a bad thing. Sometimes it's how you end up exactly where you're meant to be.</p>

        <h2>What matters to us</h2>
        <p>Lost Hiker is about good coffee, but it's also about making something ourselves and contributing, in our own small way, to the community we call home.</p>
        <p>We roast in small batches, keep experimenting, listen to the people drinking our coffee, and try to make something we're proud to share.</p>
        <p>For now, every batch is roasted right here in Sayward and shared close to home.</p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>Roasted in Sayward for wandering minds and wandering kinds.</p>
          <p class="blockquote-coda">Where it goes from here? We'll see where the trail leads.</p>
        </blockquote>

        <p>If you have questions about our coffee or want to place an order, <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>. We're not hard to find.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="values-strip">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="values-grid">
        <div class="value">
          <div class="value-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌖</div>
          <h3>Small batch</h3>
          <p>Every roast is done in small quantities to maintain quality and consistency. We'd rather roast more often than compromise a batch.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="value">
          <div class="value-icon" aria-hidden="true">◈</div>
          <h3>Traceable sourcing</h3>
          <p>We buy through importers who work directly with farms. We know the region, the farm, and often the variety and process.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="value">
          <div class="value-icon" aria-hidden="true">◇</div>
          <h3>Roasted to order</h3>
          <p>Coffee is better fresh. We roast when orders come in rather than sitting on inventory. Your bag is as fresh as it gets.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: 5rem 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .page-intro {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--mid);
    max-width: 680px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .story-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 380px 1fr;
    gap: 5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .sticky-image {
    position: sticky;
    top: 90px;
  }

  .story-image img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 2px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .story-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .story-text h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .story-text h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: none;
  }

  .story-text p {
    color: var(--mid);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .story-text a {
    color: var(--green);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--green);
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 0 2px 2px 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  blockquote p {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.1rem !important;
    color: var(--cream) !important;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  blockquote .blockquote-coda {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.97rem !important;
    color: var(--mid) !important;
  }

  /* Values strip */
  .values-strip {
    background-color: var(--surface);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 4rem 0;
    margin-top: 4rem;
  }

  .values-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .value {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .value-icon {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--green);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .value h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .value p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--mid);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .story-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }

    .sticky-image {
      position: static;
    }

    .values-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .values-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
